('127.112.d.8.A',3,'A thermostat''s function is to:','["Store air", "Create heat", "Sense temperature and control equipment", "Filter water"]'::jsonb,2,'Controls the system.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.A',4,'A thermostat is typically located:','["Over a heating register", "Outdoors in the rain", "In direct sunlight", "On an interior wall away from drafts and sun"]'::jsonb,3,'Placement affects accuracy.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.B',4,'A bimetal thermostat senses temperature using:','["Two metals that expand differently", "Gas", "Radio", "A battery"]'::jsonb,0,'Bimetal bends.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.C',3,'Before removing an old thermostat, the technician should:','["Cut wires randomly", "Turn off power to the system", "Leave the power on", "Remove the furnace"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevent shorts.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.C',4,'Thermostat wires are labeled with letters such as R, W, and Y to show the:','["Weight", "Brand of the wire", "Function of each terminal", "Age"]'::jsonb,2,'Terminal codes.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.D',3,'A basic control system includes a sensor, a controller, and a:','["Brick", "Roof", "Foundation", "Controlled device"]'::jsonb,3,'Sense, decide, act.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.D',4,'In a control loop, feedback tells the controller:','["How the system is responding", "The owner''s name", "The color of the room", "The cost of the unit"]'::jsonb,0,'Closed loop.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.E',3,'Controls that use compressed air to operate are called:','["Manual", "Pneumatic", "Electronic", "Hydraulic"]'::jsonb,1,'Pneumatic uses air.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.E',4,'A relay is an example of an:','["Manual valve", "Optical control", "Electromechanical control", "Pneumatic control"]'::jsonb,2,'Coil and contacts.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.F',3,'A systematic approach to troubleshooting starts with:','["Guessing", "Replacing parts at random", "Doing nothing", "Gathering information about the complaint"]'::jsonb,3,'Information first.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.F',4,'After finding and fixing a fault, the technician should:','["Verify the system works properly", "Leave immediately", "Skip checks", "Break something else"]'::jsonb,0,'Confirm repair.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.G',3,'Manufacturer troubleshooting charts are found in the unit''s:','["Shipping label", "Service literature", "Brochure photo", "Warranty card only"]'::jsonb,1,'Use the factory info.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.G',4,'A wiring diagram attached inside the panel helps the technician to:','["Order lunch", "Count fins", "Trace circuits", "Paint the cover"]'::jsonb,2,'Diagrams guide diagnosis.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.H',3,'A technician isolates a no-power problem by first checking the:','["Fuel price", "Filter color", "Duct size", "Main power supply and disconnect"]'::jsonb,3,'Start at the source.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.H',4,'If the control transformer secondary has no voltage but the primary has voltage, the transformer is:','["Likely bad", "New", "Overloaded", "Working"]'::jsonb,0,'No output with input.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.I',3,'A tool used to check for voltage in HVAC work is a:','["Tape measure", "Multimeter", "Plumb bob", "Hammer"]'::jsonb,1,'Meters measure electricity.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.J',3,'When checking a motor winding for continuity, power should be:','["Reversed", "Doubled", "Off", "On"]'::jsonb,2,'Ohm checks need power off.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.J',4,'A winding that reads very high resistance to ground when it should be isolated is:','["Burned", "Grounded", "Shorted", "Good"]'::jsonb,3,'Isolation to ground is good.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.K',3,'A cooling unit with a running fan but no compressor may have a bad:','["Contactor or run capacitor", "Drain pan", "Filter", "Duct"]'::jsonb,0,'Compressor circuit check.','original'),
('127.112.d.8.K',4,'When a contactor coil gets 24 volts but the contacts do not close, the likely fault is:','["A low charge", "A defective contactor", "A dirty filter", "A kinked duct"]'::jsonb,1,'Replace the contactor.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.A',3,'In a gas furnace sequence, a call for heat first starts the:','["Filter", "Humidifier", "Draft inducer", "Gas valve open"]'::jsonb,2,'Pre-purge.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.A',4,'The blower on a gas furnace starts after the heat exchanger warms up, controlled by a:','["Drain", "Spark", "Filter", "Timed delay or fan switch"]'::jsonb,3,'Prevents cold air.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.B',3,'On a ladder diagram, switches are shown in series with the load to indicate they:','["All must close for the load to run", "Do nothing", "Are decorative", "Operate in any order"]'::jsonb,0,'Series logic.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.B',4,'A limit switch in a furnace control circuit opens when temperature is:','["Zero", "Too high", "Normal", "Too low"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety shutoff.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.C',3,'A hot surface igniter lights a burner by:','["Making a spark in air", "Burning oil", "Glowing hot enough to ignite gas", "Using a pilot flame"]'::jsonb,2,'Hot surface.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.C',4,'A standing pilot burner stays:','["Off until needed", "Underwater", "Cold", "Lit continuously"]'::jsonb,3,'Always on.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.D',3,'Instruments used for gas heat troubleshooting include a multimeter and a:','["Manometer", "Ruler", "Hammer", "Metronome"]'::jsonb,0,'Gas pressure measure.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.D',4,'A combustion analyzer helps check the furnace for:','["Water pH", "Carbon monoxide and oxygen levels in the flue", "Voltage only", "Room color"]'::jsonb,1,'Combustion test.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.E',3,'When using a manometer on a gas valve, connect it to the valve''s:','["Vent", "Door", "Pressure tap", "Drain"]'::jsonb,2,'Test port.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.E',4,'After checking gas pressure, the technician must:','["Leave it open", "Smell for gas only", "Heat the tap", "Close the test port and check for leaks"]'::jsonb,3,'Leak check.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.F',3,'If a furnace lights briefly and shuts off, a likely cause is a:','["Dirty flame sensor", "New thermostat", "Full filter", "Cold room"]'::jsonb,0,'Sensor needs cleaning.','original'),
('127.112.d.9.F',4,'A furnace that short cycles on the high limit often has:','["A cold room", "Restricted airflow", "A new filter", "Too much fuel"]'::jsonb,1,'Overheats.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.A',3,'A good troubleshooting approach for cooling systems begins by:','["Pulling the compressor", "Replacing parts first", "Verifying the complaint and checking the basics", "Waiting a week"]'::jsonb,2,'Start simple.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.A',4,'The first checks on a cooling system with no cold air are the thermostat, power, and:','["Brand of unit", "Roof", "Paint", "Air filter"]'::jsonb,3,'Basic checks.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.B',3,'A problem where the compressor hums but does not start is likely:','["Electrical", "Filter", "Duct size", "Refrigerant color"]'::jsonb,0,'Hard start indicator.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.B',4,'Low suction pressure with a frosted evaporator coil often points to:','["Cold weather", "Low airflow or low charge", "Wide ducts", "High charge"]'::jsonb,1,'Mechanical symptom.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.C',3,'Many manufacturers provide a troubleshooting chart that lists:','["Jokes", "Weather", "Symptoms, causes, and fixes", "Prices"]'::jsonb,2,'Use the chart.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.C',4,'A service facts label on the unit gives:','["Local news", "Owner''s address", "Lunch menu", "Operating data and wiring"]'::jsonb,3,'Factory info.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.D',3,'A technician measures superheat using a temperature probe and a:','["Pressure gauge", "Ruler", "Hammer", "Level"]'::jsonb,0,'Superheat needs P and T.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.D',4,'Subcooling is measured on the:','["Flue", "Liquid line", "Return duct", "Gas line"]'::jsonb,1,'Liquid-line reading.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.E',3,'A dirty condenser coil typically causes:','["Low head pressure", "No change", "High head pressure", "Frozen indoor coil"]'::jsonb,2,'Poor heat rejection.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.E',4,'Restricted metering device symptoms include a cold liquid line and:','["High voltage", "Normal operation", "High suction pressure", "Low suction pressure"]'::jsonb,3,'Restriction.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.F',3,'A basic safety rule when servicing cooling units is to:','["Lock out power before opening panels", "Remove guards", "Work live always", "Ignore labels"]'::jsonb,0,'Lockout first.','original'),
('127.112.d.10.F',4,'Refrigerant liquid on skin can cause:','["Rash from heat", "Frostbite", "Nothing", "Sunburn"]'::jsonb,1,'Liquid refrigerant freezes tissue.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.A',3,'A heat pump in heating mode moves heat from:','["Fuel to air", "Ground to roof", "Outdoors to indoors", "Indoors to outdoors"]'::jsonb,2,'Even cold air has heat.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.A',4,'The reversing valve in a heat pump changes:','["Duct shape", "Filter", "Voltage", "The direction of refrigerant flow"]'::jsonb,3,'It switches modes.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.B',3,'A heat pump that uses the earth or water as its heat source is a:','["Geothermal heat pump", "Furnace", "Air-source unit", "Boiler"]'::jsonb,0,'Ground source.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.B',4,'A split-system heat pump has indoor and outdoor sections connected by:','["Wire only", "Refrigerant lines", "Hoses of water", "Ducts only"]'::jsonb,1,'Line set.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.C',3,'A closed-loop geothermal system circulates:','["Air", "Oil", "Antifreeze solution in buried pipe", "Natural gas"]'::jsonb,2,'Sealed loop.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.C',4,'An open-loop geothermal system uses:','["Sand", "Roof air", "Gasoline", "Well or surface water"]'::jsonb,3,'Water source.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.D',3,'Besides the compressor, a heat pump has an outdoor coil, an indoor coil, and a:','["Reversing valve", "Spark plug", "Heat anticipator", "Chimney"]'::jsonb,0,'Heat pump parts.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.D',4,'The accumulator on a heat pump protects the compressor from:','["Dust", "Liquid refrigerant returning", "Noise", "High voltage"]'::jsonb,1,'Prevents slugging.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.E',3,'Electric strip heat in a heat pump system is used as:','["A humidifier", "Primary cooling", "Supplemental or backup heat", "A filter"]'::jsonb,2,'Backup heat.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.E',4,'During defrost, the heat pump may energize strip heat to:','["Save energy", "Cool the coil", "Add humidity", "Prevent cold air from blowing indoors"]'::jsonb,3,'Tempers the air.','original'),
('127.112.d.11.F',3,'COP stands for coefficient of:','["Performance", "Production", "Power", "Pressure"]'::jsonb,0,'COP is efficiency ratio.','original')
